From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pcDuino3B Armbian CI <noreply@github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun7i: add LinkSprite pcDuino3B

Add a separate device tree for pcDuino3B instead of changing the
pcDuino3 description.  The boards share their A20 base design, while the
pcDuino3B uses the A20 RGMII pin group and rgmii-id mode.  This
configuration has been validated on the target pcDuino3B at 1000Mb/s
Full Duplex with an RTL8211E PHY at MDIO address 1.

Keep the registered linksprite,pcduino3 compatible followed by the A20
SoC fallback.  There is no pcDuino3B-specific compatible in the current
sunxi board binding, and inventing one would fail DT schema validation.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile                 |  1 +
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dts | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -182,3 +182,4 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_MACH_SUN7I) += \
-	sun7i-a20-wits-pro-a20-dkt.dtb
-
+	sun7i-a20-wits-pro-a20-dkt.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_MACH_SUN7I) += sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dtb
+
 # Enables support for device-tree overlays for all pis
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dts
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3b.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-or-later OR MIT)
+/*
+ * LinkSprite pcDuino3B board-level differences from pcDuino3.
+ */
+
+#include "sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "LinkSprite pcDuino3B";
+};
+
+&gmac {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&gmac_rgmii_pins>;
+	phy-mode = "rgmii-id";
+};
--
2.51.0
